{"files":[{"content":"/*\n  Quicksort\n*/\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <limits.h>\n#include <openssl/md5.h>\n\n/*\n * Prototypes\n */\nvoid srandnum(int seed);\ndouble randnum(void);\nint *generate_case(int N);\ndouble drand(int xmin, int xmax);\nvoid swap(int *toorder, int i, int j);\nint partition(int *toorder, int lo, int hi);\nvoid _quicksort(int *toorder, int lo, int hi);\nvoid quicksort(int *toorder, int N);\nint is_sorted(int *toorder, int N);\nstatic void quicksort_impl(int *toorder, int lo, int hi, int depth, int use_tasks);\nstatic int sort_depth_limit(int count);\nstatic int median_of_three_value(int a, int b, int c);\nstatic void partition_three_way(int *toorder, int lo, int hi, int *equal_lo, int *equal_hi);\nstatic void insertion_sort(int *toorder, int lo, int hi);\nstatic void sift_down(int *toorder, int lo, int root, int count);\nstatic void heapsort_range(int *toorder, int lo, int hi);\n\n/*\n * A generic pRNG\n */\n#define MY_RAND_MAX 0x7FFFFFFF\n\n#define RANDNUM_W 521288629\n#define RANDNUM_Z 362436069\n#define INSERTION_CUTOFF 24\n#define TASK_CUTOFF 8192\n#define PARALLEL_CUTOFF 65536\n\nunsigned int randum_w = RANDNUM_W;\nunsigned int randum_z = RANDNUM_Z;\n\nvoid srandnum(int seed)\n{\n    unsigned int w, z;\n    w = (seed * 104623) & 0xffffffff;\n    randum_w = (w) ? w : RANDNUM_W;\n    z = (seed * 48947) & 0xffffffff;\n    randum_z = (z) ? z : RANDNUM_Z;\n}\n\ndouble randnum(void)\n{\n    unsigned int u;\n    randum_z = 36969 * (randum_z & 65535) + (randum_z >> 16);\n    randum_w = 18000 * (randum_w & 65535) + (randum_w >> 16);\n    u = (randum_z << 16) + randum_w;\n    return (abs(u));\n}\n\n/*\n * Main function\n */\nint main(int argc, char *argv[])\n{\n    int N = 0;\n    int *our_list = NULL;\n\n    //The input provides the case size\n    scanf(\"%d\", &N);\n    if (N <= 0) {\n        printf(\"Error: please, provide the case size.\\n\");\n        return 1;\n    }\n\n    //Generate the case\n    our_list = generate_case(N);\n    if (our_list == NULL) {\n        printf(\"Error: case instantiation failed.\\n\");\n        return 1;\n    }\n\n    //Do the thing\n    quicksort(our_list, N);\n\n    if (is_sorted(our_list, N) == 1) {\n        printf(\"Error, for some reason list is still unsorted.\\n\");\n        return 1;\n    }\n\n#ifdef COMPUTE_MD5_PROBLEM\n    //Compute MD5 Checksum for problem identification\n    MD5_CTX c;\n    unsigned char out[MD5_DIGEST_LENGTH];\n    MD5_Init(&c);\n    MD5_Update(&c, our_list, N * sizeof(int));\n    MD5_Final(out, &c);\n    for (int n = 0; n < MD5_DIGEST_LENGTH; n++) {\n        printf(\"%02x\", out[n]);\n    }\n#endif\n    printf(\"\\n\");\n\n    //Clean up\n    free(our_list);\n\n    return 0;\n}\n\n/*\n * Public API\n */\nvoid quicksort(int *toorder, int N)\n{\n    if (N < 2)\n        return;\n\n    if (N < PARALLEL_CUTOFF) {\n        _quicksort(toorder, 0, N - 1);\n        return;\n    }\n\n    int depth = sort_depth_limit(N);\n#pragma omp parallel\n    {\n#pragma omp single\n        quicksort_impl(toorder, 0, N - 1, depth, 1);\n    }\n}\n\n/*\n * Internal serial entry point retained for callers of the original helper.\n */\nvoid _quicksort(int *toorder, int lo, int hi)\n{\n    if (lo >= hi)\n        return;\n    quicksort_impl(toorder, lo, hi, sort_depth_limit(hi - lo + 1), 0);\n}\n\nstatic int sort_depth_limit(int count)\n{\n    int depth = 0;\n    while (count > 1) {\n        count >>= 1;\n        depth += 2;\n    }\n    return depth;\n}\n\nstatic int median_of_three_value(int a, int b, int c)\n{\n    int temp;\n    if (a > b) {\n        temp = a;\n        a = b;\n        b = temp;\n    }\n    if (b > c) {\n        temp = b;\n        b = c;\n        c = temp;\n    }\n    if (a > b) {\n        temp = a;\n        a = b;\n        b = temp;\n    }\n    return b;\n}\n\nstatic void partition_three_way(int *toorder, int lo, int hi, int *equal_lo, int *equal_hi)\n{\n    int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;\n    int pivot = median_of_three_value(toorder[lo], toorder[mid], toorder[hi]);\n    int less = lo;\n    int current = lo;\n    int greater = hi;\n\n    while (current <= greater) {\n        if (toorder[current] < pivot) {\n            swap(toorder, less, current);\n            ++less;\n            ++current;\n        } else if (toorder[current] > pivot) {\n            swap(toorder, current, greater);\n            --greater;\n        } else {\n            ++current;\n        }\n    }\n\n    *equal_lo = less;\n    *equal_hi = greater;\n}\n\nstatic void insertion_sort(int *toorder, int lo, int hi)\n{\n    for (int i = lo + 1; i <= hi; ++i) {\n        int value = toorder[i];\n        int j = i;\n        while (j > lo && toorder[j - 1] > value) {\n            toorder[j] = toorder[j - 1];\n            --j;\n        }\n        toorder[j] = value;\n    }\n}\n\nstatic void sift_down(int *toorder, int lo, int root, int count)\n{\n    while (root < count / 2) {\n        int child = root * 2 + 1;\n        if (child + 1 < count && toorder[lo + child] < toorder[lo + child + 1])\n            ++child;\n        if (toorder[lo + root] >= toorder[lo + child])\n            return;\n        swap(toorder, lo + root, lo + child);\n        root = child;\n    }\n}\n\nstatic void heapsort_range(int *toorder, int lo, int hi)\n{\n    int count = hi - lo + 1;\n    if (count < 2)\n        return;\n\n    for (int start = count / 2; start > 0;) {\n        --start;\n        sift_down(toorder, lo, start, count);\n    }\n    for (int end = count - 1; end > 0; --end) {\n        swap(toorder, lo, lo + end);\n        sift_down(toorder, lo, 0, end);\n    }\n}\n\n/*\n * In-place three-way introsort. Large partitions can run as disjoint OpenMP\n * tasks; serial work recurses only on the smaller side and iterates on the larger.\n */\nstatic void quicksort_impl(int *toorder, int lo, int hi, int depth, int use_tasks)\n{\n    while (lo < hi) {\n        int count = hi - lo + 1;\n        if (count <= INSERTION_CUTOFF) {\n            insertion_sort(toorder, lo, hi);\n            return;\n        }\n        if (depth <= 0) {\n            heapsort_range(toorder, lo, hi);\n            return;\n        }\n\n        int equal_lo, equal_hi;\n        partition_three_way(toorder, lo, hi, &equal_lo, &equal_hi);\n        int next_depth = depth - 1;\n        int left_lo = lo;\n        int left_hi = equal_lo - 1;\n        int right_lo = equal_hi + 1;\n        int right_hi = hi;\n        int left_size = equal_lo - lo;\n        int right_size = hi - equal_hi;\n        int small_lo, small_hi, small_size;\n        int large_lo, large_hi, large_size;\n\n        if (left_size <= right_size) {\n            small_lo = left_lo;\n            small_hi = left_hi;\n            small_size = left_size;\n            large_lo = right_lo;\n            large_hi = right_hi;\n            large_size = right_size;\n        } else {\n            small_lo = right_lo;\n            small_hi = right_hi;\n            small_size = right_size;\n            large_lo = left_lo;\n            large_hi = left_hi;\n            large_size = left_size;\n        }\n\n        if (use_tasks && count >= TASK_CUTOFF && small_size > 1 &&\n            large_size >= TASK_CUTOFF) {\n#pragma omp task firstprivate(toorder, large_lo, large_hi, next_depth, use_tasks)\n            quicksort_impl(toorder, large_lo, large_hi, next_depth, use_tasks);\n            quicksort_impl(toorder, small_lo, small_hi, next_depth, use_tasks);\n            return;\n        }\n\n        if (small_size > 1)\n            quicksort_impl(toorder, small_lo, small_hi, next_depth, use_tasks);\n        lo = large_lo;\n        hi = large_hi;\n        depth = next_depth;\n    }\n}\n\n/*\n * Swap two values.\n */\nvoid swap(int *toorder, int i, int j)\n{\n    int temp = toorder[i];\n    toorder[i] = toorder[j];\n    toorder[j] = temp;\n}\n\n/*\n * Partition decision retained for callers of the original helper.\n */\nint partition(int *toorder, int lo, int hi)\n{\n    int b = lo;\n    int r = (int) (lo + (hi - lo) * (randnum() / MY_RAND_MAX));\n    int pivot = toorder[r];\n    swap(toorder, r, hi);\n    for (int i = lo; i < hi; i++) {\n        if (toorder[i] < pivot) {\n            swap(toorder, i, b);\n            b++;\n        }\n    }\n    swap(toorder, hi, b);\n    return b;\n}\n\n/*\n * Check if elements are in non-decreasing order\n */\nint is_sorted(int *toorder, int N)\n{\n    for (int i = 1; i < N; i++) {\n        if (toorder[i] < toorder[i - 1]) {\n            return 1;\n        }\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n\n/*\n * Generate a case\n */\nint *generate_case(int N)\n{\n    int i;\n    int *ret = NULL;\n\n    // Make case generation reproducible\n    srandnum(0);\n\n    // Allocate memory\n    ret = (int *) malloc(N * sizeof(int));\n    if (ret == NULL) {\n        printf(\"Error: some malloc won't work.\\n\");\n        return NULL;\n    }\n    // Get pseudo-random positive integer values\n    for (i = 0; i < N; i++) {\n        ret[i] = drand(0, INT_MAX);\n    }\n    return ret;\n}\n\n/*\n * A pseudo-random number between two positive integer values\n */\ndouble drand(int xmin, int xmax)\n{\n    return xmin + (xmax - xmin) * randnum() / MY_RAND_MAX;\n}\n","path":"src/quicksort.c"}],"hypothesis":"Combining median-of-three three-way partitions, insertion sort for tiny ranges, and a depth-limited heapsort fallback should keep serial sorting efficient and robust. For large arrays, disjoint OpenMP tasks above a cutoff can exploit the four-core target without changing generated values or output.","notes":"One integrated candidate for full controller evaluation; no correctness or timing result is claimed.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":["aaf96556279640d7","4c628d637a2e4123","52c9b35ec0474a42"],"transformations":["Use median-of-three pivots and a three-way partition so equal keys are excluded from recursive work.","For arrays of at least 65536 elements, enter an OpenMP parallel/single region and create tasks for sufficiently large disjoint partitions, using an 8192-element cutoff.","Bound partition depth and fall back to heapsort when the limit is reached.","Finish ranges of at most 24 elements with insertion sort; otherwise recurse on the smaller side and iterate over the larger side when not tasking it."]}